Refining a module whose inherited method has a `:|` statement with an automatically chosen trigger that selects a member of a receiver, such as `s.tail` or `m.Keys`, no longer crashes with a `NullReferenceException` in `DetectUnderspecificationVisitor` under `--type-system-refresh`, and no longer reports a spurious type error under the legacy resolver when the receiver is a generic call such as `Id(m).Keys`.
